What:		/proc/<pid>/jank_info
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru
Description:
	Per-task opt-in scheduler-latency accounting used by the Oplus
	health/performance stack. Writing 1 starts accounting for the selected
	task. Writing 0 stops accounting and clears that task's accumulated
	runnable, running, uninterruptible, I/O-wait, binder, futex, mutex, and
	rwsem timing. Reading returns the accumulated values in milliseconds.

What:		/proc/oplus_healthinfo/alloc_wait
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru
Description:
	Read-only foreground, UX, and total page-allocation wait statistics,
	including high/low wait counts, maxima, allocation orders, and the
	healthinfo control, logging, and trigger state.

What:		/sys/module/memory_monitor/parameters/ion_wait_h_ms
What:		/sys/module/memory_monitor/parameters/ion_wait_l_ms
What:		/sys/module/memory_monitor/parameters/ion_wait_log_ms
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru
Description:
	Read/write thresholds, in milliseconds, for Oplus ION allocation-wait
	accounting and optional healthinfo logging. Donor defaults are 500, 100,
	and 1000 milliseconds respectively.
